# Intended production egress policy

This scaffold cannot enforce an Azure Container Apps SandboxGroup network
policy locally. The production `Microsoft.App/SandboxGroups` deployment must:

1. Default-deny all outbound traffic.
2. Allow HTTPS (TCP 443) only to `__EGRESS_ALLOW_DOMAIN__`. Do not use a
   wildcard domain.
3. Allow only the platform DNS path required to resolve that FQDN.
4. Explicitly deny private address ranges, Azure metadata endpoints, and every
   other public destination.
5. Disable payload capture. Emit only create/execute/delete lifecycle events,
   duration, and exit status.
6. Auto-delete each sandbox after the verdict is read.

Before a demo, verify the policy from inside a sandbox: a call to
`__EGRESS_ALLOW_DOMAIN__` must succeed, while an unrelated HTTPS endpoint must
fail. Treat failure of either negative test as a release blocker.
